cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use sci-rag-kit in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "sci-rag-kit: a DIY GraphRAG factory for scientific domains"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Sustainability Software Lab, Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sustainability-software-lab/sci-rag-kit"
license: BSD-3-Clause
keywords:
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - knowledge graph
  - scientific software
  - pgvector
  - evaluation
abstract: >
  A template repository for building grounded, citation-backed
  question-answering systems over scientific document collections:
  structure-aware ingestion, five fused retrieval layers over PostgreSQL
  (dense vectors, full-text, knowledge-graph traversal, community
  summaries, HyDE), fail-closed license scoping, a blind-judge
  evaluation harness, and serving over REST and MCP. Generalizes the
  retrieval methodology developed for the PISCES bioprocess platform at
  Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory; created in collaboration with
  the University of Washington Scientific Software Engineering Center
  under the Schmidt Sciences VIS program.
